  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-14T16:43:48.179Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm not sure if this request has been done before, but I thought of this over the past 2 days.\n\nDesktop users have been getting more and more options lately, such as the inclusion of gestures through the Function keys and the ability to crouch/prone, why not make a feature where they can point their arm forward, like if they were holding an item? I have friends who would want a feature like this but not want to go through a ton of silly workarounds to get their avatar to point forward. I'm sure it wouldn't be hard either, you can probably just reuse the script that brings the character's arm up.",
